Because in classic WoW, leveling and questing isn't the only thing that matters — most warlocks are seen in endgame PvE raiding, where the voidwalker's Sacrifice shield and threat generation are far more valuable than the succubus's damage and CC. The succubus is better for solo leveling, but the voidwalker is the practical choice for group content, which is where warlocks spend most of their time. [end of text]


